__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"IMAMS",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const t=[{id:'abu-hanifa',name:'Imam Abu Hanifa',arabic:'\u0627\u0644\u0625\u0645\u0627\u0645 \u0623\u0628\u0648 \u062d\u0646\u064a\u0641\u0629',title:'The honest merchant scholar',minutes:3,color:'#0F5C4D',paragraphs:['An-Nu\u2019man ibn Thabit, known as Abu Hanifa, was born in Kufa, Iraq, in 80 AH (699 CE). He was a cloth merchant known for his honesty in business.','He became one of the greatest scholars of fiqh. He taught his students to discuss each question together and reason from the Quran and Sunnah. His school, the Hanafi madhhab, is followed by many Muslims today, especially in South Asia and Turkey.','When the caliph al-Mansur ordered him to become chief judge, he refused, and he was put in prison. He passed away in Baghdad in 150 AH (767 CE).'],lesson:'Knowledge and honesty go together, in the masjid and in business.',question:'What did Abu Hanifa sell for a living?',refs:['Born 80 AH, Kufa','Died 150 AH, Baghdad','Students: Abu Yusuf and Muhammad al-Shaybani']},{id:'malik',name:'Imam Malik',arabic:'\u0627\u0644\u0625\u0645\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u0627\u0644\u0643',title:'The imam of Madinah',minutes:3,color:'#7A4E1D',paragraphs:['Malik ibn Anas was born in Madinah in 93 AH (711 CE), the city of the Prophet \ufdfa, and spent his life there.','He wrote al-Muwatta, one of the earliest books of hadith and fiqh. It is reported that he would make ghusl and wear his best clothes before teaching hadith, out of respect for the words of the Prophet \ufdfa.','His school, the Maliki madhhab, spread across North and West Africa. He passed away in Madinah in 179 AH (795 CE).'],lesson:'Show respect for knowledge, and for the words of the Prophet \ufdfa most of all.',question:'What famous book did Imam Malik write?',refs:['Born 93 AH, Madinah','Died 179 AH, Madinah','Book: al-Muwatta']},{id:'shafii',name:'Imam al-Shafi\u2019i',arabic:'\u0627\u0644\u0625\u0645\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0634\u0627\u0641\u0639\u064a',title:'The student who memorized young',minutes:3,color:'#2E4A7A',paragraphs:['Muhammad ibn Idris al-Shafi\u2019i was born in Gaza in 150 AH (767 CE), the same year Abu Hanifa died. He grew up poor with his mother in Makkah.','It is reported that he memorized the Quran by age seven and the Muwatta by age ten. He travelled to Madinah to study with Imam Malik himself.','He wrote ar-Risalah, the first book to lay out the principles of fiqh. His school, the Shafi\u2019i madhhab, is followed widely in Egypt, East Africa and Southeast Asia. He passed away in Egypt in 204 AH (820 CE).'],lesson:'Start young, learn from the best teachers, and never stop studying.',question:'Who was Imam al-Shafi\u2019i\u2019s famous teacher in Madinah?',refs:['Born 150 AH, Gaza','Died 204 AH, Egypt','Book: ar-Risalah']},{id:'ahmad',name:'Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal',arabic:'\u0627\u0644\u0625\u0645\u0627\u0645 \u0623\u062d\u0645\u062f \u0628\u0646 \u062d\u0646\u0628\u0644',title:'Firm in the trial',minutes:3,color:'#5A3A78',paragraphs:['Ahmad ibn Hanbal was born in Baghdad in 164 AH (780 CE). He was a student of Imam al-Shafi\u2019i and travelled far to collect hadith.','He compiled al-Musnad, a huge collection of tens of thousands of hadith.','Rulers of his time tried to force scholars to say the Quran was created, not the word of Allah. Imam Ahmad refused. He was imprisoned and whipped, but he stayed firm. He passed away in Baghdad in 241 AH (855 CE), and a huge crowd attended his funeral.'],lesson:'Stand by the truth with patience, even when it costs you.',question:'What did Imam Ahmad refuse to say?',refs:['Born 164 AH, Baghdad','Died 241 AH, Baghdad','Book: al-Musnad']},{id:'bukhari',name:'Imam al-Bukhari',arabic:'\u0627\u0644\u0625\u0645\u0627\u0645 \u0627\u0644\u0628\u062e\u0627\u0631\u064a',title:'The most trusted book after the Quran',minutes:3,color:'#1F6E8C',paragraphs:['Muhammad ibn Isma\u2019il al-Bukhari was born in Bukhara, Central Asia, in 194 AH (810 CE). It is reported that he lost his sight as a child and his mother made dua until it came back.','He memorized hadith from a young age and travelled across the Muslim world to learn from hundreds of teachers.','He spent about sixteen years compiling his Sahih. It is reported that he made wudu and prayed two rakahs before adding each hadith. Muslims see Sahih al-Bukhari as the most authentic book after the Quran. He passed away near Samarkand in 256 AH (870 CE).'],lesson:'Be careful and sincere with what you pass on to others, especially about the Prophet \ufdfa.',question:'How many years did Imam al-Bukhari spend on his Sahih?',refs:['Born 194 AH, Bukhara','Died 256 AH, near Samarkand','Book: Sahih al-Bukhari']},{id:'muslim',name:'Imam Muslim',arabic:'\u0627\u0644\u0625\u0645\u0627\u0645 \u0645\u0633\u0644\u0645',title:'The careful student',minutes:2,color:'#3E6B3A',paragraphs:['Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj was born in Nishapur, in today\u2019s Iran, around 204 AH (820 CE). He studied with many scholars, including Imam al-Bukhari.','He compiled Sahih Muslim, the second most trusted hadith book, known for its careful order and for keeping every chain of narrators exact.','He passed away in Nishapur in 261 AH (875 CE).'],lesson:'Learning from good teachers and respecting them is part of seeking knowledge.',question:'Which great hadith scholar did Imam Muslim study with?',refs:['Born about 204 AH, Nishapur','Died 261 AH, Nishapur','Book: Sahih Muslim']}]},1366,[]);
